    "updated_at": "2017-05-22T04:18:59Z",
    "body": "My understanding is that the parser is responsible for the lowercasing; the mixed-case name is never even passed to DOM's element-creation algorithms, so even if DOM wanted to store it somewhere, it couldn't.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, if you are in an XML document, then the parser won't lowercase, I believe. So in that case it'll just be available as `.localName`.",
